\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid10816525 
\par 
\par }{\cf0\ulc0\insrsid10816525 Which one has more overhead, a repeater or a bridge? Explain your answer. [3]
\par }{\b\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid212751 
\par Answer:}{\b\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid10816525 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid212751 {\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid212751\charrsid212751 A bridge has more overhead than a repeater. A bridge processes the packet at two
\par }{\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid212751 l}{\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid212751\charrsid212751 ayers}{\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid212751  }{\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid212751\charrsid212751 ; a repeater processes a frame at only one layer. A bridge needs to search a
\par table and find the forwarding port as well as to regenerate the signal; a repeater
\par only regenerates the signal. In other words, a bridge is also a repeater (and more); a
\par repeater is not a bridge}{\b\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid212751\charrsid212751 .}{\b\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid212751 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10816525 {\b\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid212751 
\par }{\b\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid10816525 
\par Question No: 37      ( Marks: 3 )
