\par 
\par }{\cf0\ulc0\insrsid10816525 How parity bits are counted in VRC error detection method technique in case of odd parity generator?
\par }{\cf0\ulc0\insrsid4288833 
\par }{\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid4288833\charrsid212751 Answer}{\cf0\ulc0\insrsid4288833 :}{\cf0\ulc0\insrsid10816525 
\par }{\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid2056738\charrsid212751 For example:
\par }{\f0\insrsid2056738\charrsid212751 We want to TX the binary data unit 1100001}{\f0\cf0\ulc0\insrsid2056738\charrsid212751 
\par }\pard \qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4288833 {\f0\insrsid4288833\charrsid212751 Adding together the number of 1\rquote s gives us 3, an odd number
\par }\pard \qj \li360\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid10165 {\f0\insrsid4288833\charrsid212751 Before TX, we pass the data unit through a parity generator, which counts the 1\rquote 
s and appends the parity bit (1) to the end 
\par The total number of 1\rquote s is now 4, an even number 
\par The system now transfers the entire expanded across the network link 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4288833 {\fs20\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842 \~}{\f0\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842 
\par }\pard \qj \li360\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid10165 {\fs20\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842 When it reaches its destination, the RX puts all 8 bits through an even parity checking function}{
\f0\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842  
\par }{\fs20\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842 If the RX sees 11100001, it counts four ones, an even number and the data unit passes}{\f0\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842  
\par }{\fs20\insrsid10165  W}{\fs20\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842 hen the parity checker counts the 1\rquote s, it gets 5 an odd number}{\f0\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842  
\par }\pard \qj \li360\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid15533819 {\fs20\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842 The receiver knows that an error has occurred somewhere and therefore rejects the whole unit}{
\f0\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842  
\par }{\fs20\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842 Some systems may also use ODD parity checking}{\f0\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842  
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid4288833 {\fs20\insrsid4288833\charrsid11883842 The principal is the same as even parity}{\cf0\ulc0\insrsid4288833 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10816525 {\cf0\ulc0\insrsid4288833 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par 
